    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Personalization-Specialist_R312079": {
      "title": "Personalization Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description Opportunity:   Join the Aviation and Aerospace vanguard!    Step into a dynamic role with Embry Riddle Aeronautical University, where innovation meets opportunity. Be part of a leading institution that’s at the forefront of aviation, aerospace, and STEM education. We offer an exciting environment, cutting-edge projects, and the chance to influence tomorrow. Ready to make a difference? Take flight with Embry-Riddle and explore this diverse career opportunity today. Position Overview: The Personalization Specialist plays a key role within the marketing team, primarily focusing on creating dynamic content and building logic for enhanced personalization across university-wide enrollment communications. This position combines strong writing skills with data-driven decision-making, ensuring that email and SMS campaigns resonate with a diverse student audience. The specialist is responsible for designing, building, and testing content that aligns with specific audience segments, such as traditional-age students, adult learners, transfer students, and international students, among others. The role requires close collaboration with the Associate Director of Enrollment Communication to identify opportunities for enhanced personalization, utilizing tools like Salesforce Marketing Cloud and AMPscript to craft tailored experiences that maximize engagement and conversion rates. In addition to content creation, the Personalization Specialist is also responsible for continuously monitoring the performance of dynamic content, using audience performance analytics to refine and optimize messaging strategies. This includes identifying underperforming segments, diagnosing issues, and implementing adjustments to improve campaign results. The specialist also plays a crucial role in ensuring content consistency and streamlining processes across communication efforts, working with various university stakeholders—including academic leaders and program coordinators—to align messaging with institutional goals. A strong technical foundation in HTML, AMPscript, and a deep understanding of audience segmentation and behavioral data analysis are essential for success in this role. Please note: This position is in-person at one of our residential campus locations (Daytona Beach, Fl or Prescott, AZ). This position is not remote or hybrid Key job functions include: Write static and dynamic content and build email communications to create personalized experiences for diverse prospective student audiences, including traditional, adult, transfer, international, and military students Optimize and manage dynamic content using conditional logic, AMPscript, and HTML Recommend and implement email communication strategies Develop policies and best practices for prospect student population segmentation Work with the Marketing CRM Analysts to assess the current usage of system data to determine areas for improvement, as well as the implementation of Salesforce Education Cloud Accountable for recommending the best ways for Enrollment Management (EM) to use email segmentation Analyze audience performance metrics, identify under-performing segments, diagnose root causes, and implement enhancements to improve the overall ROI of marketing efforts Maintain detailed records of dynamic content versions and create new version catalogs for each academic year in Sharepoint About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Marketing or Communications 3-5 years of professional experience (preferably in email marketing or other marketing/communications roles)   Required skills, knowledge, abilities: Demonstrated expertise in writing and editing static and dynamic email content with an eye for detail Experience with building dynamic content logic rules to create personalized email/SMS experiences Strong technical and data interpretation skills with experience analyzing key performance metrics Experience Salesforce, Marketing Cloud, & Microsoft Applications; AMPscript experience is highly preferred To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312079 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote---Virginia/Assistant-Director-Recruitment-and-Outreach_R312044": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Recruitment and Outreach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     Embry-Riddle Student Recruitment is seeking a dynamic individual to join their team as the Assistant Director of Student Recruitment (ADR). The ADR is responsible for regional recruitment, outreach, public relations and marketing to meet enrollment goals for their designated region/market. This person provides civilian and military prospective students and leads with relevant information regarding University programs and services and next steps towards enrollment through virtual, phone, email communication. The role oversees and supervises assigned Regional Recruitment Counselor(s) (RCs) to ensure territory performance and goals are met and evaluates the effectiveness of all recruitment and engagement activities and events. The ADR will be responsible for developing a regional strategy to represent the University in a variety of forums to meet and recruit prospective students, promote programs, establish contacts at local, regional and national industry, college, transfer and military fairs. This person will select, plan and execute event attendance, and conduct University presentations regionally to individuals and groups of prospective students and businesses, both in-person and virtually. The ADR fosters relationships with appropriate contacts to include, Education Service Officers (ESO) (where applicable), Human Resource Managers, Training Managers, and Enrollment/Marketing liaisons, as applicable. This role also works closely with other departments to ensure coordination of all recruitment and admissions activities and ensures that all University policies and procedures are enforced. This is a remote role and moderate travel is required . Please note that due to staffing needs, this position is open to all candidates currently residing in or planning to relocate to any of the following states: CT, DE, DC, IN, MD, MA, MI, NH, NJ, OH, PA, RI, VI, VT, WV. ​ This position will require travel time away from the office. May work evenings, weekends and/or holidays as required. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree Analytical skills with an in-depth knowledge of information systems and technical expertise with Microsoft operating systems, Access, Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook/email, and Internet end-user applications Proven track record for consistently meeting deadlines with the ability to tactfully handle difficult situations and maintain composure under pressure, often under tight deadlines. Must be a dynamic, motivated, and enthusiastic individual with professional recruitment experience in higher education. Must be able to provide excellent customer service to coworkers, staff, students, faculty, and customers. Must demonstrate exceptionally strong verbal and written communication skills. Must demonstrate a high standard of personal conduct, professionalism, and integrity and the ability to maintain confidentiality is vital. Must be able to work independently with minimal supervision and demonstrate a willingness to seek guidance and direction as necessary for the performance of duties. Must be able to recognize and deal with priorities, recognize, and perform duties not directly assigned. Must be able to investigate, problem-solve and take corrective action. Moderate travel required. Preferred Qualifications Master's Degree Marketing/advertising experience Prior experience in higher education administration, marketing, and/or counseling Aviation experience Requirements to be able to drive a university vehicle: Must possess and maintain a valid US driver’s license. Must meet the University’s standards for approved drivers. Unacceptable driving records (as stated in the Use of Equipment and Vehicles Procedure 1.17) include the following (for three years from the date of each occurrence): Three (3) or more at-fault accidents and/or moving violations in the previous 36 months. Two (2) or more at-fault accidents or two (2) or more moving violations in the past year. Conviction for driving while impaired (DWI, DUI within the last five (5) years). Conviction for death by vehicle, hit and run, racing, careless and reckless driving, implied consent in the previous five (5) years. Serious violations result in immediate disqualification and revocation of driver privileges. The following are examples of serious violations​: Speeding over 15 mph of the posted limit, driving under the Influence of alcohol or drugs, leaving the scene of an accident, reckless or careless. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312044 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Dean-of-Students--Daytona-Beach-Campus_R312073": {
      "title": "Dean of Students, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity: Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is now seeking a dynamic and experienced individual to join our team as Dean of Students at the Daytona Beach Campus. Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Student Success, and overseeing functional areas including Housing & Residential Life, Counseling Center, Health Services, Fitness Center, Center for Faith and Spirituality, Student Engagement, Organizations, and Student Union activities, the Dean of Students provides leadership and vision for the development, implementation, and coordination of a comprehensive student affairs program. The Dean of Students is responsible for fostering a supportive and inclusive campus environment that enhances student learning, development, and engagement. This position plays an essential role in shaping Embry-Riddle’s student experience by providing leadership, strategic direction, and accountability for the administration, development, communication, assessment, and improvement of students’ services and experiences in alignment with the university and campus mission and strategic plans. Key Responsibilities: Leadership and Administration: Provide strategic direction and leadership to the Division of Student Affairs. Develop and implement policies, procedures, and programs that support student success and well-being. Supervise and evaluate the performance of student affairs staff. Manage the budget and resources allocated to student affairs programs and services. Serve as a key member of the university’s leadership team, contributing to institutional planning and decision-making. Collaborate with Dean of Students at the Prescott and Worldwide campuses to ensure a seamless student affairs experience across the university. Student Advocacy and Support: Advocate for student needs and interests within the university administration. Oversee student conduct processes and ensure fairness and consistency in disciplinary actions. Develop and maintain programs that promote student mental health and wellness. Responsible for conflict resolution and primary problem-solver for issues involving students. Works closely with Campus Safety, Title IX, faculty, department chairs, advisors, legal counsel, and others to resolve issues, including after hours and on weekends. Provide leadership and guidance when student-related crises occur and manage these crises at the campus- and individual level with discretion, and respect for students, families, and the institution. Community Building: Foster an inclusive campus community that respects and values diversity. Develop programs and initiatives that promote student engagement and leadership. Collaborate with academic departments and other university offices to enhance the student experience. Oversee the development of residential life programs that support student learning and community development. Compliance and Assessment: Ensure compliance with federal, state, and local regulations related to student affairs. Conduct regular assessments of student services and programs to ensure they meet the needs of the student population. Use data to inform decision-making and improve student services. Communication and Support Communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, parents, and external stakeholders. Serve as a liaison between students and the university administration. Represent the university at various functions, conferences, and meetings. About Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University:   For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Education: Minimum: Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, Counseling, or a related field is required. A Doctorate is preferred. Experience: Minimum of 5-10 years of progressively responsible experience in student affairs or a related field, with significant leadership and supervisory experience. Demonstrated experience in crisis management, student conduct, and student support services. Demonstrated leadership ability and decision making to develop an effective team. Skills and Abilities: Strong leadership and organizational skills. Demonstrated ability in budget and resource allocation and strategic planning and a clear understanding of the academic process and its relationship to student issues. Demonstrated ability to successfully manage multiple projects simultaneously and to formulate and execute effective action plans. Ability to work well in an intense, fast-paced environment. Able to recognize and/or recruit talented staff. Expertise in diffusing and resolving conflict while remaining empathetic to all parties involved. Must have strong mediation skills. Demonstrated cultural awareness. Knowledge of student affairs/services programs and operations. Ability to effectively supervise and evaluate employees. Ability to analyze data that is relevant to the work of the Student Affairs Division and identify statistical trends. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, communication, and leadership skills and the ability to work collaboratively and effectively with students, faculty, staff, and senior administration. Networking skills are essential. Recent training in leadership competencies in student affairs, especially dispute resolution, social justice and inclusion, law and policy, student conduct, and judicial affairs. Knowledge of relevant laws, regulations, and best practices in student affairs, including Title IX, FERPA, ADA, and Clery Act compliance. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312073. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
