    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Flight-Record-Coordinator_R311892-1": {
      "title": "Flight Record Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University - Daytona Beach is seeking a detail-oriented and collaborative Flight Record Coordinator to serve as a vital link between the Office of the Registrar and the Daytona Beach and Prescott Flight Departments. Reporting to the University Registrar, this unique cross-functional role is responsible for ensuring the accurate exchange of data between academic and flight operations systems, maintaining regulatory compliance, communicating student status information to partner offices and supporting internal and external audits, record discrepancy review and resolution of record issues. The Coordinator will be responsible for ensuring appropriate messaging is departed to students through established communication channels. Additionally, this individual will maintain procedures, identify process gaps, and support improvements related to flight training records and academic records. The ideal candidate will be skilled in student data management, understand FAA, TSA, DOE and VA regulations as they pertain to flight training programs, and be experienced in higher education processes involving academic record management, satisfactory academic progress, registration, and scheduling. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.  Qualifications Qualifications   Bachelor's Degree. A minimum of 1 to 3 years of relevant work experience is required. Type of work-related experience: Administrative/Compliance/Higher Ed/Flight Ops Strong knowledge of FAA, DOE, TSA and VA regulations and academic policies.  Excellent attention to detail, problem-solving skills, and organizational abilities.  Proficiency with student information systems (e.g., PeopleSoft) and flight scheduling (ETA) software.  Experience with Microsoft Access and Excel strongly desired To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311892 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/Marketing-Communications-Specialist_R312046": {
      "title": "Marketing Communications Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity:    As a Marketing Communications Specialist, you will play a crucial role in crafting compelling narratives for prospective students through innovative and impactful communication strategies. This entry level position offers an opportunity to blend creativity with strategic thinking, collaborating with internal stakeholders to shape the future of our marketing initiatives. Key Responsibilities: Collaborative Strategy Development: Engage in dynamic collaboration with internal stakeholders to formulate cutting-edge communication strategies. Interface seamlessly with digital, social media, and creative services teams to drive cohesive cross-team initiatives. Needs Assessment and Goal Establishment: Proactively identify communication needs and establish strategic goals in partnership with internal stakeholders. Assess the viability of requests, ensuring alignment with overarching marketing objectives. Resourceful Print and Digital Management: Liaise with marketing team members when requests necessitate print or digital resources. Collaborate closely with the Digital Communication Specialist to craft compelling email copy and gather email assets. Independent Storytelling: Independently source captivating success stories from students, faculty, and alumni. Craft engaging written materials such as blog posts, newsletters, and articles, determining the optimal distribution channels for maximum impact. Organization and Maintenance: Uphold and manage degree-specific playbooks, content databases, communication flows, and other material repositories. Ensure efficient organization and accessibility of materials to support streamlined communication processes Adaptive Responsibilities: Embrace a dynamic work environment with the readiness to undertake various assigned duties to contribute to the overall success of the team and organization About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.         Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications   ​ Education: Bachelor's degree in Communications, Marketing, or a related field. Experience: Proven track record in marketing and communications, showcasing successful strategies. Technical Skills: Proficient in Microsoft Applications with expertise in leveraging them for effective communication. Familiarity with Salesforce and Marketing Cloud. Demonstrated writing and editing skills for crafting polished content. Multichannel Expertise: Experience in print, email, digital, and social media platforms. Strategic Decision-Making: Ability to make editorial decisions aligning with recruitment lifecycles, university policies, and goals. Interpersonal Skills: Excellent interpersonal skills for effective collaboration with diverse stakeholders. Innovative Thinking: Innovative thinker with the ability to challenge existing methods. Work Style: Independent worker and self-starter, thriving in both autonomous and collaborative environments. Organizational Skills: Highly organized, deadline-oriented, and a skilled communicator with a strong grasp of writing principles. Motivation: Self-motivated with the ability to seek guidance when necessary.   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312046. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Accounts-Payable-Specialist_R312051": {
      "title": "Accounts Payable Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University's Accounts Payable team is currently looking for an Accounts Payable Specialist. Reporting to the Accounts Payable Manager, the Accounts Payable Specialist will be responsible for the accounting and administrative duties related to the efficient processing and maintenance of accounts payable transactions. The position’s primary function is to control expenses by receiving, processing, verifying and reconciling invoices and expense reports while maintaining compliance with IRS regulations and University policies and procedures. Additional responsibilities include administrative support of university faculty/staff and vendor maintenance and account reconciliation. Examples of Key Responsibilities and Opportunities for the Accounts Payable Specialist: Analyze payment requests to ensure compliance with university business expense policies. Audit and acquire supporting documentation for all expenses. Code invoices, vouchers, expense reports, check requests, etc., with correct codes conforming to standard accounting procedures to ensure proper entry into the University’s financial system. Monitor account balances, track expenses, and produce monthly financial reports. Develop and maintain assigned supplier portfolio. Investigate and resolve problems associated with processing invoices and purchase orders. Reconcile supplier accounts by identifying errors in posting or omissions, applying appropriate accounting standards. Generate scheduled payment files and remittance information for all University payment methods, including positive pay, ACH, ePayables, and employee expense and travel reimbursements. Maintain supplier records with proper IRS reporting documentation. Facilitate IRS 1099-MISC and 1099-NEC information reporting compliance. Prepare fiscal year-end closing procedures and provide reporting to the University Accounting Office.   About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Compensation     The hourly rate for this role is   up to  $21.65 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Candidate Profile: Exceptional personal qualities: A reputation for integrity and the highest ethical standards; sound judgment; enthusiasm for the mission; creativity in solving problems; collegial style and strong desire to be an integral part of the Embry-Riddle community. Customer focus: Dedicated to meeting the expectations and requirements of internal and external customers, including Procurement Services and University vendors. Establishes and maintains effective relationships while representing the integrity of the Controller’s Office. Systems and technology: Functional knowledge of information technology and its appropriate use for effective and efficient delivery of accounting and financial reporting. Experience with Workday and/or Oracle preferred. Proficiency using Microsoft Office Suite. Education and experience:  Associate’s degree or completion of program of 18+ months after high school. Area of study: accounting, finance, banking or related field.     To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312051 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Grounds-Supervisor_R308738": {
      "title": "Grounds Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Opportunity:  The Grounds Supervisor is responsible for the effective management of all landscaping and grounds maintenance activities. This role requires expertise in irrigation systems, pest control for turf and ornamentals, and disease identification in plants. The supervisor will also handle material ordering, scheduling, and at times perform hands-on tasks alongside the team. A key aspect of this role includes testing irrigation systems and conducting yearly evaluations for staff. The successful candidate will be required to obtain an LLO pesticide license within the first 90 days of employment. Key Responsibilities: Team Leadership and Supervision: Supervise and mentor grounds maintenance staff, providing guidance and support to enhance skills and efficiency. Conduct annual performance evaluations for team members, identifying areas for improvement and professional development. Landscaping and Maintenance: Oversee the maintenance and enhancement of landscaped areas, ensuring adherence to quality and design specifications. Participate in hands-on maintenance tasks when necessary to demonstrate best practices. Irrigation Management: Design, install, and maintain irrigation systems, ensuring efficient water usage and optimal plant health. Regularly test and evaluate irrigation systems for functionality and efficiency. Pest Control and Disease Management: Identify pests and diseases affecting turf and ornamental plants, implementing integrated pest management strategies. Develop treatment plans for pest control and disease management in compliance with regulations. Material Ordering and Inventory Management: Order necessary landscape supplies, including plants, herbicides, fertilizers, and equipment. Manage inventory levels to ensure all required materials are available for maintenance tasks. Scheduling and Project Management: Create and manage work schedules for grounds maintenance staff to ensure timely completion of tasks. Prioritize and assign daily activities based on project needs and environmental conditions. Record Keeping and Reporting: Maintain accurate records of maintenance activities, pest control applications, and inventory management. Prepare reports on grounds maintenance operations for management review. Safety and Compliance: Ensure all operations comply with safety regulations and industry standards. Conduct safety training sessions and promote a culture of safety among team members. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off :   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions :   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Compensation     The hourly range for this role is   up to  $20.00 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent; degree in horticulture, landscape management, or related field preferred. Minimum of 5 years in grounds maintenance or landscaping, with at least 3 years in a supervisory role Required licenses, certificates, and/or security clearances: Obtain an LLO pesticide license within the first 90 days of employment, ensuring compliance with state and local regulations. Relevant certifications in pesticide application and irrigation management preferred. Candidates will be expected to obtain a Limited Lawn and Ornamental Pesticide License (LLO) by the State of Florida within the first 90 days of employment. We are excited to share that Embry-Riddle will cover the cost for the Grounds Supervisor to obtain a Limited Lawn and Ornamental License. Must possess and maintain a valid, US driver’s license. Must meet the University’s standards for approved drivers. Unacceptable driving records (as stated in the Use of Equipment and Vehicles Procedure 1.17) include the following (for three years from the date of each occurrence): Three (3) or more at-fault accidents and/or moving violations in the previous 36 months. Two (2) or more at-fault accidents or two (2) or more moving violations in the past year. Conviction for driving while impaired (DWl, DUl within the last five (5) years). Conviction for death by vehicle, hit and run, racing, careless and reckless driving, implied consent in the previous five (5) years. Serious violations result in immediate disqualification and revocation of driver privileges. The following are examples of serious violations ​ : Speeding over 15 mph of the posted limit, driving under the Influence of alcohol or drugs, leaving the scene of an accident, reckless or careless driving, Use of vehicle in (drug trafficking, reckless homicide, soliciting), unlawful use of weapons, driving under suspension or revocation, fleeing a police officer, vehicle theft, Improper or illegal lane change, following too close, and passing a stopped school bus while stop sign is engaged. Required knowledge, skills, and abilities: Comprehensive understanding of landscaping practices, turf management, and ornamental horticulture. Proficient in irrigation systems design, maintenance, and testing. Familiarity with pest control methods and plant disease identification. Strong leadership and team management abilities. Excellent organizational and scheduling skills. Proficient in computer applications for scheduling, record keeping, and inventory management. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Detail-oriented with a commitment to high-quality standards. Working Conditions: Ability to work outdoors in various weather conditions. Physical ability to lift and carry equipment up to 50 pounds. Flexibility to work occasional weekends and holidays as needed. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R308738. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Research-Engineer--College-of-Engineering--Daytona-Beach-Campus_R312030": {
      "title": "Research Engineer, College of Engineering, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University’s College of Engineering invites applications for an Aerospace Engineering Research Engineer to support faculty and student research within the Department of Aerospace Engineering at the Daytona Beach Campus. This hands-on position plays an important role in the safe and effective operation of aerospace laboratories, workshops, and wind-tunnel facilities while helping researchers transform ideas into working experimental systems. The successful candidate will combine strong engineering fundamentals with practical fabrication, computer-aided design, laboratory operations, and safety expertise. The role regularly collaborates with faculty, graduate and undergraduate students, researchers, university partners, and external scientists and engineers. Key Responsibilities Coordinate and support instructional, research, student-project, demonstration, and tour activities in aerospace laboratories, workshops, and wind-tunnel facilities. Assess requests for laboratory and shop use, advise on feasibility and potential modifications, and maintain a master schedule for shared facilities. Support aerospace engineering faculty and students in designing, building, modifying, and troubleshooting experimental apparatus and research equipment. Use computer-aided design and engineering tools to create parts, assemblies, drawings, simulations, and laboratory experiments. Perform machining, woodworking, welding, painting, plumbing, and sheet-metal fabrication as needed to support research and instruction. Train and guide students in the safe use of laboratory, machine-shop, and wind-tunnel equipment; provide design and manufacturability guidance. Maintain, inspect, and repair a broad range of laboratory equipment, machines, instrumentation, and facilities; coordinate outside repair or installation work when needed. Maintain equipment and supply inventories and assist with purchasing, specifications, installation planning, documentation, and budget-related activities. Serve as a safety advocate by implementing and reinforcing University and applicable occupational safety procedures, maintaining safety documentation, and identifying potential hazards. Assist with classes, laboratories, tours, and other training activities, and remain current through relevant conferences, training, and professional development. About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day. Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Aerospace Engineering or a related engineering field. Three to five years of related experience, including experience in experimental aerodynamics, engineering research, laboratory operations, or a closely related area. Advanced CAD experience, part design, assembly design, kinematics, finite element analysis, and engineering drawings, with emphasis on current GD&T standards. Knowledge of mechanics, solid mechanics, aerodynamics, thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, advanced computational methods, and nonlinear finite element methods. Knowledge of aviation and aerospace instrumentation, sensors, and wind-tunnel operations. Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work productively with faculty, students, researchers, industry professionals, and technical and nontechnical colleagues. Demonstrated team-building, leadership, organization, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment with limited supervision and to manage multiple priorities safely and responsibly. Experience working with and guiding young adults in laboratory, workshop, research, or educational settings. United States citizenship. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Aerospace Engineering or a related engineering field. Industry or research experience relevant to aerospace laboratories, experimental aerodynamics, fabrication, or wind-tunnel operations. Application process/requirements Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312030 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
