    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/A-P-Technician_R309208": {
      "title": "A&P Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Discover Your Future with Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University!       Embry-Riddle: A Global Leader in Aviation and Aerospace        With vibrant campuses in Daytona Beach, FL and Prescott, AZ, plus a Worldwide network across approximately 120 locations, Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. For over 95 years, we've been pioneering education in STEM fields, serving over 11,600 residential students and 19,200 globally in the 2023-24 academic year with cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space.      Opportunity:     Join the Aviation and Aerospace vanguard!    Step into a dynamic role with Embry Riddle Aeronautical University, where innovation meets opportunity. Be part of a leading institution that’s at the forefront of aviation, aerospace, and STEM education. We offer an exciting environment, cutting-edge projects, and the chance to influence tomorrow. Ready to make a difference? Take flight with Embry-Riddle and explore this diverse career opportunity today.     Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking an experienced Aircraft Maintenance Technician to perform top-quality maintenance and repairs on our University aircraft fleet. In this role, you'll work with minimal oversight, following all Federal Aviation Regulations and industry standards to ensure the airworthiness of our aircraft. Key Responsibilities: Perform authorized maintenance, preventive maintenance, and unscheduled repairs on aircraft, engines, and appliances. Assist the Shift Lead with maintenance operations and inventory control. Complete documentation for maintenance forms, inspection reports, and aircraft logbooks. Respond to maintenance needs promptly, including on weekends and holidays, as required. Familiarity with FAA regulations, approved inspection programs, and airworthiness standards. Attention to detail and commitment to safety. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!   Generous Time Off: Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day.  Personal Leave: Relax with 12 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.  Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.  Application process/requirements To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R309208 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full Resume Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees:  Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .   Qualifications High school (or GED) level ability in spelling, grammar, basic composition, and math. Read and comprehend instructions, write information, and complete simple forms. Current Airframe and Powerplant Certificate required with no violations. One to three years of related work experience. Required skills, knowledge, abilities: Working knowledge of FAR 145, 91 and 43. Aircraft Maintenance experience in maintaining light general aviation aircraft preferred. Basic PC Software Skills (e.g. spreadsheet, word processing & database etc.) PowerPoint, Word, Outlook/email, and Internet end-user applications preferred. Excellent communication skills required."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/Academic-Advisor_R312021": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) seeks a dynamic, student-centered, and forward-thinking Academic Advisor to provide visionary leadership   The Academic Advisor for Undergraduate Students at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University, Prescott Campus, provides comprehensive academic guidance and student support within a rigorous, aviation and STEM focused learning environment. This role supports students from matriculation through graduation by assisting with academic planning, course selection, degree requirements, university policies, and institutional resources. Advisors work closely with faculty, student services, and campus partners to promote student success, retention, and timely degree completion while upholding Embry-Riddle’s academic standards and mission. The advisor serves as a primary point of contact for undergraduate students, offering individualized advising that aligns academic goals with career aspirations in aviation, aerospace, engineering, security, and related fields. Responsibilities include monitoring academic progress, interpreting degree audits, supporting students on academic probation or at risk, and providing guidance on registration, transfer credit, internships, and experiential learning opportunities. The position also contributes to orientation programs, outreach initiatives, and campus events, and maintains accurate advising records in compliance with university and accreditation requirements. This role requires strong knowledge of Embry-Riddle Prescott academic programs, excellent communication skills, and the ability to support a diverse student population in a fast paced, mission driven campus environment. Primary Job Functions, Duties, or Accountabilities: Foundations of Academic Advising Assist students with registration, course selection, academic planning, schedule adjustments, and other program updates. Refer students to appropriate university resources when questions arise. Engage with the advising team for cross training Enforce university policies and procedures, ensuring students understand degree requirements, transfer credit policies, and the importance of co-curricular engagement.  Collaborate with faculty and other stakeholders to track student progress, identify at-risk students, and provide timely outreach. Work with specified cohorts based off of your committee codes.  Ensure clear communication with fellow advisors by informing them of any interactions or work conducted with their assigned students. Uphold strict confidentiality and ethical advising practices.  Advisors must stay within their designated scope of responsibility and avoid involvement in decision-making outside their role.  Professional Responsibilities & Campus Engagement Attend all required department meetings, training sessions, and professional development opportunities in person. Participate in committees and campus initiatives as assigned. Actively contribute to UNIV101 workshops. Serve as a liaison to other departments (Admissions, Registrar, Housing, etc.), ensuring clear and appropriate communication. Accurately maintain student records using university-approved technology and systems. Support & Outreach Assist in planning, organizing, and executing university-wide events such as New Student Orientation, Open House, and Spring Preview Day. Represent the advising team at events, fostering connections with prospective and current students, parents, and campus partners. Ensure that event participation aligns with the department’s mission and objectives. Student Outreach & Retention Strategies Conduct targeted outreach to first-year students and students identified as academically at-risk. Implement proactive strategies to engage and support students in achieving academic success. Maintain detailed documentation of outreach efforts and follow-up actions. Collaborate with relevant campus colleges and departments to ensure a coordinated approach to student success. About us   For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professiona l staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.  Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.  Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.       Compensation   The annual salary range for this role is   up to  $ 46,000. The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in STEM subject, psychology, sociology, counseling, communication, education or other related field 1-3 of experience in Student Support or Administrative   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311806. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full CV   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .        Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/Flight-Scheduling-Data-Analyst_R311989": {
      "title": "Flight Scheduling Data Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) is seeking a detail-oriented, analytical, and customer-focused Flight Scheduling Data Analyst to support flight training operations at the Prescott Campus. The Flight Scheduling Data Analyst serves as the primary administrator and subject matter expert for the university's flight scheduling and training management systems. This position is responsible for managing Flight Training Software platforms, analyzing and reporting operational data, supporting scheduling functions, and ensuring system integrity across multiple flight operations applications. Working independently and collaboratively with flight department leadership, instructors, scheduling personnel, and student employees, the Flight Scheduling Data Analyst develops reports, maintains system permissions, manages software configurations, and supports strategic initiatives through data-driven decision making. This position also serves as a key resource for specialized projects, documentation development, instructor system training, and operational support functions. The successful candidate will possess strong analytical abilities, technical aptitude, organizational skills, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic flight training environment. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Aviation, Business Analytics, Management Information Systems, or a related field. One (1) to three (3) years of experience supporting software systems, scheduling operations, data management, or aviation-related operations. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Word, Outlook, and PowerPoint. Experience working with databases, reporting tools, and data analytics. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills. Ability to interpret data and generate reports that support operational decision-making. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy. Ability to work independently while managing multiple priorities and deadlines. Demonstrated customer service and interpersonal skills with the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff. Ability to learn, administer, and support specialized software applications. Must be able to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound professional judgment. Preferred Qualifications Experience in a collegiate aviation, flight training, or higher education environment. Familiarity with ETA/Talon Systems Flight Training Software. Experience administering or supporting CloudAhoy, FlightOps, Clipboard, SplashBI, or similar operational software platforms. Knowledge of flight scheduling, resource management, or aviation operations. Experience creating dashboards, reports, and business intelligence analytics. Experience training users on software systems and technical processes. Experience supporting operational, scheduling, or workforce management systems. Knowledge of FAA flight training environments and aviation education programs. Experience supervising or coordinating student employees. Advanced Excel skills, including pivot tables, data analysis, and reporting functions. Experience managing software permissions, user access controls, and system configurations. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311989 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/San-Diego-California/Assistant-Professor-of-the-Practice-of-Applied-Aerospace-Science--Remote---US-_R311655": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of the Practice of Applied Aerospace Science (Oceanside, CA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The College of Aviation (COA) at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University Worldwide (ERAU-W) is seeking an Assistant Professor of the Practice of Applied Aerospace Science. A requirement of this position is to teach 9-week cohorts of transitioning military members 18 semester hours of aviation maintenance courses. The position will require conducting face-to-face classes, 8 hours per day at the ERAU WW Oceanside campus, CA, with an approximate a 10-week break between cohorts. As an additional requirement, the successful candidate must remain current in the needs and requirements of the aviation maintenance industry to provide cohort students mentorship that would lead to successful employment. About the College of Aviation The mission of the College of Aviation is to develop and provide graduate and undergraduate academic programs that enable students to excel in the multi-disciplinary field of aerospace; in the aeronautics industry, in the military, and in the local, state and federal government organizations connected to aerospace programs. The mission also includes assessing program outcomes and using these assessments to update courses and programs. About us For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!    Generous Time Off: Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: Candidates must have an earned Master’s Degree and a Federal Aviation Administration Airframe and Powerplant Certificate. A background in providing military technical training is desired, but not required. The candidate must also have a strong desire to assist transitioning military members into successful civil aviation maintenance careers. Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311655. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statement of teaching philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Vicenza-Italy/Assistant-Campus-Director_R312020": {
      "title": "Assistant Campus Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       The Assistant Campus Director supports the daily operations of the campus while helping deliver an exceptional experience for students, faculty, and community partners. This position plays a key role in student recruitment, retention, advising, and campus communications while building strong relationships with civilian and military organizations. The Assistant Campus Director serves as a campus leader and assumes responsibility for campus operations in the absence of the Campus Director and/or Associate Campus Director, ensuring University policies, procedures, and service standards are consistently maintained. Key Responsibilities Support the daily administrative and operational activities of the campus and serve as acting campus leadership when needed. Promote University programs and services through recruitment activities, college fairs, community outreach, military briefings, and other marketing efforts. Build and maintain effective relationships with local civilian organizations, military representatives, and Education Services Officers. Provide student services including academic advising, counseling, unofficial evaluations, degree mapping, and student account follow-up. Support student recruitment and retention efforts through regular communication with prospects, applicants, new students, and continuing students. Maintain accurate student records and data in Campus Solutions and Campus Imaging. Complete registration, end-of-term, student account, and other campus actions accurately and on schedule. Monitor enrollment trends and assist with identifying opportunities to support campus growth and student success. Ensure University policies, procedures, and operational standards are consistently followed. Assist with monitoring campus budgets, expenditures, and financial activities while safeguarding University assets. Maintain campus audit readiness and support financial and operational reporting requirements. Provide administrative support, including phones, email, mail, supply orders, faculty support, and daily campus operations. Ensure classrooms, facilities, and EagleVision spaces are prepared and maintained for instructional use. Prepare accurate reports, correspondence, and documentation for University and external agencies. Participate in required training and effectively utilize University systems, tools, and resources. Demonstrate sound judgment, problem-solving skills, professionalism, and a commitment to excellent student service. About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Compensation     The hourly rate for this role is   up to  $17.00 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Education Associate’s degree or completion of a post-secondary program of at least 18 months following high school. Ability to read and comprehend instructions and simple forms. Experience 0–1 year of related work experience. Experience providing student support. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Knowledge of information systems and common end-user applications. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Access, Outlook/email, and Internet applications. Excellent customer service and interpersonal communication skills. Working knowledge of office procedures and equipment. Ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in higher education or counseling. Experience in marketing, advertising, or recruitment. Aviation-related experience or knowledge. Individual Logistical Support (ILS) experience or background To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312020 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
