    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Academic-Evaluator_R312013": {
      "title": "Transfer Academic Evaluator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) seeks a student-centered, detail-oriented Transfer Academic Evaluator to support prospective and current transfer students at our Daytona Beach Campus. Reporting to the Associate Registrar, this position serves as a primary resource for transfer credit evaluation and helps students understand how previously completed coursework may apply toward an Embry-Riddle degree. The Transfer Academic Evaluator serves as a primary point of contact for the EAB Transfer Portal, providing course equivalency determinations and academic degree information to prospective students. This role evaluates progress toward degree completion, educates pre-applicant students on academic programs, policies and procedures, and supports excellence in student service throughout the transfer process. In this role, you will maintain accurate transfer course equivalencies and student information system data, collaborate closely with Admissions and technical teams, and identify opportunities to improve processes and functionality. Key responsibilities include: Respond to prospective student inquiries regarding transfer credit and the applicability of previously completed coursework toward ERAU degree programs. Evaluate previously earned course credit and determine ERAU course equivalencies. Generate detailed progress-toward-degree reports through the EAB Transfer Portal. Build and maintain course equivalency rules within the Student Information System. Maintain Student Information System tables and review expired course equivalency rules for accuracy. Partner with Admissions to support Transfer Portal processes and ensure academic policies and course equivalency requirements are followed. Develop employee training materials and business process manuals for the EAB Transfer Portal. Collaborate with technical staff to improve processes, streamline functionality and produce ad hoc reports. Co-facilitate transfer student sessions during Orientation and assist with Transfer Student Orientation and Admissions Preview Day. Update individual Academic Advising Reports (AAR) based on program or catalog changes, advanced standing or placement, course substitutions, equivalency exams and flight certificates. About Us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year. Compensation   The annual salary range for this role is  up to  $43,888. The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.  Qualifications Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in education, counseling, organizational management, communication, or a related field . Minimum of 1–3 years of related work experience . Excellent organizational skills and initiative, with the ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Ability to organize and prioritize multiple responsibilities. Proficiency with computers, email/internet, Microsoft applications and imaging systems. Knowledge of accepted practices at higher education institutions and academic policies, procedures, standards and curricula. Familiarity with non-traditional sources of college-level advanced standing credit, including American Council on Education military credit recommendations and national examinations such as CLEP and DANTES. Experience advising or interacting with students and the ability to troubleshoot student issues. Familiarity with Registrar's Office operations and industry best practices. Ability to work weekend or evening hours as needed during peak periods. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with various software solutions and/or implementing software solutions. Previous experience with SIS Campus Solutions . Application process/requirements   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the  Embry-Riddle Career Site  and search for requisition number  R311480. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Full Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees:  Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our  website .  Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Acquisitions-Technician_R311825-1": {
      "title": "Acquisitions Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) invites applicants to join   its   dynamic team   in   the   Hunt Library,   serving a diverse population of residential and online students, faculty, staff, and researchers.   Th e Acquisitions Technician   position plays   an important role   in ensuring   timely   access to Hunt Library's print and electronic collections. Working closely with the Acquisitions Librarian, library colleagues, vendors, and campus partners, you will support the ordering, receipt, invoicing, and processing of library resources that advance the university's teaching, learning, and research mission.   The successful candidate will join the Hunt Library (https://huntlibrary.erau.edu), serving the Daytona Beach, Prescott, and Worldwide Campuses, working regular business hours. The Hunt Library is committed to an inclusive,   equitable   working environment. We strive to create a collegial culture of belonging for our staff and students and welcome applicants from all backgrounds.   Primary Responsibilities   Responsibilities include, but are not limited to:   Coordinate the ordering, receiving, invoicing, and processing of print and electronic library materials while working with vendors and campus partners to resolve ordering issues.   Maintain   accurate   acquisitions,   vendor , inventory, and financial records using the Alma library   management   system and other library technologies.    Track purchase requests and communicate with   library staff   throughout the   acquisitions   process.    Assist   with collection maintenance activities, including gift materials,   serials,   leisure reading collections, repairs, and materials processing.    Prepare reports,   monitor   acquisitions   expenditures, and   assist   with budget tracking and workflow documentation.    Coordinate departmental mail distribution and maintain processing   and repair supplies.    Participate in special projects, library committees, and other duties as assigned.   About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Compensation     The hourly range for this role is  $16.00-$17.00 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Required Qualifications   High school diploma or GED.    One to three years of related work experience.    Strong written communication, grammar, basic math, and organizational skills.    Experience using Microsoft Office and standard internet applications.    Ability to work independently while managing multiple priorities.    Strong analytical, problem-solving, and attention-to-detail skills.    Ability to learn and effectively use library information systems and business applications.    Preferred Qualifications   Some   college   preferred .    Experience working in a library or similar information-centered environment.    Familiarity with   library management   systems (such as Alma), MARC records, OCLC, GOBI /YBP , EBSCONET, or other library resource management software.    Experience with ordering, invoicing,   purchasing ,   or accounts   payable workflows.    Knowledge of library acquisitions, technical services, or collection management processes.    To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311825. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
