    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/Visiting-Professor-of-Safety-Science--Prescott-Campus_R311889": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant/Associate Professor of Safety Science, Prescott Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Department of Safety Science at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University in Prescott seeks a single-term, Visiting Assistant or Associate Professor of Safety Science in the College of Aviation. This is a teaching-focused position with an expectation to teach 4 sections in the Spring 2027 semester. This position has no research expectations, although opportunities for research may be available. This position's expected start date is January 4, 2027. This position primarily focuses on teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in aviation safety (AVSF) and safety science (SFTY). The instructed courses may include the subjects of aircraft accident investigation, structural and mechanical failures in aircraft accident investigation, safety training and leadership, research methods, or occupational safety. The successful candidate will have a strong desire to focus on innovative and high-quality instruction in a collegial and collaborative environment. The successful candidate will deliver high-quality instruction, demonstrate teaching excellence, and engage in activities to enrich the academic experience and advance the field of aviation safety. About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. About the department of Safety Science, Prescott Campus The Safety Science Department at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University, Prescott, serves students at the BS and MS levels and is housed in the College of Aviation. The department features undergraduate and graduate education in aviation safety, supporting the aviation safety minor and an MS in Safety Science. The department facilities include the Robertson Aircraft Accident Investigation Lab, Aviation Safety and Security Archives, and additional lab spaces.  Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Qualifications Candidates must have an MS in Aviation, Aerospace, Safety, or a closely related field, with at least 18 credits of PhD progress in a related discipline. An earned PhD in discipline or a closely related field is preferred. Application process/requirements To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311889 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statements of teaching philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/Assistant-Director-of-Organizations-and-Orientation--Prescott-Campus_R311549": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Engagement and Student Union, Prescott Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity   Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University – Prescott is seeking an energetic, collaborative, and student-focused professional to serve as the Assistant Director of Student Engagement and Student Union within the Department of Student Engagement & Student Union (SESU). This position plays a central role in creating a vibrant campus community by supporting student involvement, leadership development, orientation programs, and student organization success. The Assistant Director will work closely with students, faculty, staff, and campus partners to provide meaningful co-curricular experiences that enhance student engagement and belonging across campus. Position Overview: The Assistant Director provides primary oversight and leadership in the following areas: Registered Student Organizations (RSOs) Student Government Association (SGA) advising Orientation and transition programs Student leadership and engagement initiatives Departmental operations and student support services Key Responsibilities: Registered Student Organizations (RSOs) Serve as the primary contact and advisor for Registered Student Organizations Manage the new RSO registration and annual re-registration processes Provide guidance and support to student organization officers and advisors Coordinate training and development opportunities, including Officer Orientation programs Maintain and update RSO resources and educational materials Oversee organization-focused programs and events, including the annual Organization Fair Support student involvement marketing and outreach initiatives Manage RSO event registration and student travel notification processes Partner with University Risk Management to review and maintain safety standards and procedures for high-risk organizations Assess RSO programs and operations to ensure effectiveness and continuous improvement Student Government Association (SGA) Serve as advisor to the Student Government Association and various SGA Service Organizations Meet regularly with student leaders to provide mentorship and operational support Attend and support open and closed SGA meetings Coordinate contracts and organizational logistics Assist with oversight of SGA budgets, project funds, and financial processes Support leadership development and organizational effectiveness among student government leaders Orientation & Transition Programs Lead the planning, development, and implementation of fall and spring Orientation programs Recruit, train, supervise, and mentor more than 40 student Orientation Leaders and Lead Orientation Leaders Manage Orientation program budgets and expenditures Coordinate with campus stakeholders to ensure seamless implementation of Orientation initiatives Collaborate with partners across Academic Affairs, Facilities, ROTC, the Chancellor’s Office, Campus Events, and other departments Participate in Campus Opening Committee planning efforts for the start of each semester Department Operations & Student Support Supervise a student assistant supporting RSO and departmental initiatives Serve as an administrator for the university’s student organization and event management software platform, Eagle Life (Campus Groups) Assist with departmental budgeting, purchasing, and operational processes Serve as a University conduct officer and oversee the RSO conduct process Collaborate on departmental initiatives related to Fraternity and Sorority Life, Leadership programs, Parent & Family Programs, Union operations, Campus-wide student engagement efforts Serve as a campus resource for event planning software and procedures, including Eagle Life and SchedulER Support departmental assessment initiatives and policy/procedure review processes Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace  As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning nearly 120 global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery. As we launch our next century, we remain committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible.  Click here to take a virtual tour of the Prescott Campus! Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!   Health Benefits:   Experience comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, along with wellness programs that include preventive care and fitness memberships. Our flexible spending and health savings accounts simplify managing healthcare costs. Join a workplace that prioritizes your health—because your journey to wellness should be rewarding! Buckle up for a healthier, happier you!   Tuition Coverage:  Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.     Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes an annual 6% gift of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period.   Generous Time Off:   Generous Time Off: Relax with 18 days of personal leave in your first year. Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day.      Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Minimum of 2 years of professional experience in Student Activities and/or advising student organizations within higher education Demonstrated ability to thrive in a fast-paced, student-centered environment Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to effectively engage students, faculty, staff, and administrators Experience coordinating, planning, and executing campus events and programs Strong problem-solving, decision-making, and organizational skills with the ability to take initiative Ability to manage multiple priorities while collaborating effectively across campus departments Commitment to supporting a diverse student population and fostering an inclusive campus community Flexibility to work evenings and weekends as needed Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration or a related field 3–5 years of professional experience advising student organizations on a college campus Direct experience working with student government organizations Knowledge of best practices in student involvement, engagement, and community building Experience using Campus Groups or similar student organization management software Experience serving as a student conduct officer Active involvement in local, state, or national professional organizations related to student activities or higher education leadership Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311549 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Scheduling-Manager_R311993": {
      "title": "Scheduling Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     The Scheduling Manager plays a key role in ensuring efficient, accurate, and student-centered course scheduling across multiple instructional modalities, including face-to-face (F2F), EagleVision Classroom (EVC), EagleVision Home (EVH), and online. This position provides an opportunity to collaborate with academic departments and Student Success Operations to align course offerings with student demand, faculty availability, and institutional priorities. The Scheduling Manager will use data, problem-solving, and cross-functional collaboration to optimize resources, identify and resolve scheduling conflicts, and support the successful delivery of academic programs. The role also provides the opportunity to oversee adjunct faculty scheduling, contracts, and payroll processes while ensuring accuracy and compliance with established academic timelines. This is an excellent opportunity for a detail-oriented and collaborative professional to make a meaningful impact on academic operations, faculty support, and the overall student experience.   Key Responsibilities Scheduling Management Create, organize, and maintain accurate course schedules across all instructional modalities, including face-to-face (F2F), online, EagleVision Classroom (EVC), and EagleVision Home (EVH). Review scheduling reports to identify discrepancies, correct errors before student enrollment, manage class cancellations, and implement appropriate course dispersal solutions. Resolve scheduling issues in accordance with established guidelines to ensure efficient, accurate, and consistent scheduling across campuses and platforms. Monitor enrollment and scheduling data to adjust course offerings based on student demand, faculty availability, and institutional needs. Department & Adjunct Faculty Coordination Collaborate with academic departments and campus administration to assign and schedule courses based on departmental needs and faculty availability. Partner with the Student Success Operations team, including Site Directors, to coordinate F2F and EVC course offerings based on student needs, faculty availability, and physical or virtual classroom capacity. Manage adjunct faculty scheduling and course assignments, ensuring timely communication of schedule changes to faculty and relevant stakeholders. Adjust course offerings as needed to accommodate changes in enrollment, faculty availability, or other operational requirements. Scheduling Timelines & Faculty Contracts Ensure compliance with established academic schedule development timelines and coordinate required scheduling activities. Manage and implement adjunct instructor contract invitations, ensuring contracts are processed accurately and within established deadlines. Coordinate faculty and adjunct payroll processes, ensuring timely and accurate compensation. Scheduling Discrepancy Resolution Identify and communicate scheduling discrepancies to academic departments and appropriate stakeholders. Collaborate with departments to resolve scheduling conflicts and ensure accurate course section offerings across modalities and campuses. Escalate unresolved or complex scheduling issues to Academic Scheduling Coordinators as appropriate. Institutional Collaboration Serve as a liaison among Academic Affairs, Instructional Design, Colleges, Student Success Operations, and other institutional areas to support accurate and conflict-free course scheduling. Collaborate with institutional partners to optimize the use of campus facilities and EVC resources. Identify and resolve conflicts involving classroom availability, virtual resources, faculty assignments, and course timing. Maintain effective communication with stakeholders to ensure scheduling decisions support institutional priorities and the student experience. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.        Compensation     The annual salary range for this role is   up to  $43,888 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.       Qualifications Qualifications Associate degree or completion of at least 18 months of post-high school education. 1–3 years of related work experience. Experience in an administrative work environment.     To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311993. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Instructional-Consultant-I_R311990": {
      "title": "Instructional Consultant I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       The Rothwell Center for Teaching and Learning Excellence (RCTLE) is seeking an Instructional Consultant I to support academic and instructional excellence across Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University–Worldwide. This position guides, mentors, and develops faculty throughout their teaching lifecycle through individualized consultation, faculty observation, professional development, and evidence-based instructional practices. The Instructional Consultant I will collaborate with faculty, college leadership, instructional designers, and university departments to strengthen teaching and learning and positively impact student success. Key Responsibilities Provide guidance, mentoring, and individualized support to new and experienced faculty. Review assigned courses and provide recommendations aligned with best practices in teaching and learning and contractual expectations. Conduct annual faculty observations and recommend resources and strategies for improvement. Research and evaluate emerging pedagogical resources and instructional technology practices. Plan, coordinate, and facilitate optional and college-specific faculty training and professional development offerings. Develop and update instructional resources based on RCTLE and college needs. Collaborate with college leadership and university departments to identify concerns, resolve issues, and develop proactive instructional solutions. Work with Instructional Designers and Course Developers to evaluate data, identify trends, and support improvements to instructional design and development. Maintain current knowledge of pedagogy, instructional technology, the scholarship of teaching and learning, and university curriculum and policies.     About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.        Compensation     The annual salary range for this role is   up to  $53,000 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Required: Master’s degree in education, educational leadership, educational administration, instructional technology, instructional design, or a related field. At least three years of teaching experience; online higher education experience is preferred. Strong administrative, research, project management, communication, and interpersonal skills. Knowledge of evidence-based teaching practices and instructional technology. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, RCTLE staff, college leadership, and university departments. Self-motivated with the ability to work independently and without close supervision. Work Environment This position is based within the ERAU-Worldwide environment and operates in a typical office setting. The role requires strong communication, collaboration, organization, independent judgment, and the ability to manage multiple tasks effectively. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311990 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Spangdahlem-Germany/Campus-Director_R311842": {
      "title": "Campus Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     The Campus Director plays a critical role in advancing student success and supporting the overall operations of a Worldwide Campus location. This position provides leadership across campus administration, student services, enrollment support, financial oversight, and community engagement while serving as a key representative of the University. The Campus Director works collaboratively with internal and external partners to deliver exceptional service to students, promote academic achievement, strengthen enrollment efforts, and ensure operational excellence. This role offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact by guiding students through their educational journey, building strong relationships within the community and military partnerships, and supporting a mission-driven environment focused on student access, retention, and degree completion. Key Responsibilities Campus Operations & Administration Oversee the daily operations of a Worldwide Campus location, ensuring effective administration, compliance with University policies, and delivery of high-quality student services. Manage campus resources, facilities, classrooms, and operational processes to ensure a safe, welcoming, and effective learning environment. Maintain accurate campus and student records while ensuring data integrity within University systems. Support audit readiness through accurate documentation, financial oversight, and adherence to University procedures. Student Advisement & Success Support Provide comprehensive academic guidance to students by assisting with program selection, degree planning, course scheduling, registration, and degree completion strategies. Monitor student progress, identify at-risk students, and provide proactive outreach and recommendations to support retention and academic success. Resolve student enrollment and academic issues while connecting students with appropriate University resources, including admissions, financial services, Veterans Affairs, and academic support services. Maintain student confidentiality and ensure compliance with applicable policies and procedures. Enrollment Management & Recruitment Outreach Partner with enrollment leadership to support campus enrollment goals and oversee the student enrollment lifecycle from prospective student engagement through graduation. Represent the University through recruitment activities, community outreach, college fairs, military briefings, networking events, and other engagement opportunities. Build and maintain strong relationships with military representatives, Education Services Officers (ESOs), local organizations, and community partners. Budget & Financial Management Assist with campus budget management, including monitoring expenditures, travel expenses, purchase reconciliation, outreach/marketing plans, and contract compliance. Safeguard University assets through inventory management, safety processes, emergency preparedness planning, and responsible resource management. Ensure campus financial operations remain accurate, organized, and prepared for review or audit. Human Resources & Team Leadership Provide leadership and support for campus employees, including recruitment, onboarding, training, development, and performance management, when applicable. Serve as a resource and liaison for HR-related processes, including position requests, performance feedback, evaluations, and employee relations matters. Foster a collaborative and service-focused campus environment that supports employee and student success. University Representation & Collaboration Represent the University in a professional and positive manner while promoting programs, services, and educational opportunities. Collaborate with University departments, campus leadership, and stakeholders to support operational goals and student outcomes. Participate in University meetings, training programs, workshops, town halls, and professional development activities. Provide feedback and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives that enhance campus operations and student experiences. U.S. citizenship or lawful permanent resident status, along with eligibility for SOFA (Status of Forces Agreement) status, is required for this position.   About us     For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professiona l staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.     Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Compensation     The annual salary range for this role is   up to  $ 50,400 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.         Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. 1–3 years of relevant professional work experience. Ability and willingness to work independently and effectively within a geographically dispersed environment. Experience providing leadership, management, and/or supervision of employees or teams. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to collaborate effectively with students, staff, faculty, and external partners in both in-person and remote environments. Excellent verbal and written communication skills with the ability to communicate effectively with diverse audiences. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain attention to detail. Ability to maintain professionalism, sound judgment, and composure while working in high-pressure or changing environments. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to evaluate information, identify solutions, and make informed decisions. Proficiency with information systems and technical applications, including Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook/email, and Access) and internet-based applications. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education administration, student services, enrollment management, marketing, or customer service. Experience supporting students in an academic advising or student success environment. Experience working with military-affiliated students, education programs, or geographically distributed campuses. Experience developing community partnerships, conducting outreach, or supporting recruitment initiatives. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311842. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full CV   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .      Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Research-and-Instruction-Librarian_R311970-1": {
      "title": "Research and Instruction Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     The Hunt Library at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) invites applications for the position of Research and Instruction Librarian serving a diverse population of residential and online students. The Research and Instruction Services Department is currently hiring for a Research and Instruction Librarian who is passionate about serving students through research consultations and instruction, developing information literacy, and engaging in creative partnerships with faculty through liaison relationships. The successful candidate will join the Hunt Library https://huntlibrary.erau.edu/, serving Daytona Beach and our Worldwide Campus of online students, working regular business hours including nights and weekends. This professional staff position reports to the Associate Director for Research and Instruction Services. Hunt Library is a forward-thinking, technologically advanced library organization on the Ex Libris ALMA ILS and offering a robust range of electronic collections and integrated library software. Duties include working as part of a team providing reference services in-person, virtual, and electronic modes, developing online learning objects, sharing in synchronous and asynchronous library instruction, and participating in collaborative team and cross-departmental assignments and special projects. No aviation or aerospace background is required: we welcome librarians from a wide variety of academic disciplines who will enjoy working with our dedicated, hardworking students. Growing the research presence and agenda is at the heart of the ERAU strategic plan, and Hunt Library provides an excellent opportunity for librarians who want to engage with the development of research skills among undergraduate and graduate students. Consider joining our team. Recent graduates and mid-career librarians are encouraged to apply. A leader in the provision of higher education in the fields of aviation and aerospace, ERAU offers regionally accredited bachelors’, masters’, and doctoral degrees. For more information on ERAU, see http://www.erau.edu/about/index.html . For more information on the Hunt Library, go to http://huntlibrary.erau.edu/about/ . Information on the new library facility is available at https://studentunion.erau.edu/. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.         Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications The Hunt Library values diversity, equity, and inclusion and is committed to hiring staff who share these values. We strive to create a collegial, inclusive culture of belonging for our staff and students, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds. Required Qualifications: · ALA-accredited master’s degree in library science or information studies. · Library reference and research assistance experience, or an interest in research librarianship as a career path. · Library instruction experience and/or an interest in developing pedagogical skills in librarianship. · Demonstrated ability to learn new technology tools and skills and remain current with emerging technologies and processes. · Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively with a diverse population of faculty/staff, students, and colleagues. · Ability to work collaboratively across library and organizational teams for projects such as collection management, promotion of library resources, and development of new library artifacts and initiatives. · Excellent analytical, interpersonal, time management, organizational and problem-solving skills. · Excellent written and oral communication skills. · Experience communicating effectively in a virtual environment. Preferred Qualifications: · Academic library experience. · Instruction or training experience and comfortable presenting to small and large groups. · Database knowledge and searching proficiency. · Experience developing online learning objects or online modules. · Experience training, supervising, or mentoring student assistants. · Experience developing, providing, or assisting with events. · Proficiency with learning management software such as Canvas. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311970. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Student-Organizations-Coordinator_R311965": {
      "title": "Student Organizations Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) seeks a dynamic, student-centered, and forward-thinking Student Organizations Coordinator to provide visionary leadership. The Student Organizations Coordinator will oversee, advise, and support the activities of Registered Student Organizations (RSOs). This position oversees campus processes for RSO event management, advising and support, as well as RSO travel.  Through a combination of advising, training, and experiential learning, students will be supported to develop leadership skills and abilities to build and maintain strong, effective organizations.  This position reports to the Director of Student Organizations and works regularly with department staff responsible for RSO finances.  This position is part of a collaborative team of professionals supporting student engagement across a wide range of areas that also include student government, campus activities, orientation, and the student union. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Compensation     The annual salary range for this role is   up to   $43,888. The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree required. A minimum of 1-3 years of experience in higher ed student affairs or event management is required.    Demonstrated experience in the areas of leadership development, advising, student development, and event management.   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311965 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/Director-of-Facilities_R311978": {
      "title": "Director of Facilities",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking an experienced and strategic Director of Facilities to lead day-to-day facilities operations for the Prescott, Arizona campus. Reporting to the Vice President for Facilities, this position provides leadership across facilities maintenance, utilities, transportation, shipping and receiving, grounds, housing maintenance, and project management. This is a highly visible leadership opportunity for a facilities professional who can balance day-to-day operational needs with long-term planning and campus priorities. The Director will work independently to evaluate facility needs, develop solutions, manage resources, oversee contractors and projects, and contribute to the continued development of the campus facilities master plan and standard operating procedures. The ideal candidate will bring strong facilities or construction leadership experience, sound judgment, financial and project management skills, and the ability to lead teams across multiple trades and service areas. This position also serves as a member of the Prescott Chancellor’s Campus Leadership Team and is an on-call role responsible for responding to after-hours facilities issues. Key Responsibilities Lead, supervise, coach, and evaluate facilities personnel across multiple trades and service areas, including electrical, plumbing, HVAC, energy management, grounds, transportation, building services, materials management, and housing maintenance. Plan, schedule, and oversee maintenance activities and external contractors to ensure campus buildings, grounds, utilities, mechanical and electrical systems, and safety and security systems are properly maintained. Develop, implement, and oversee preventative maintenance, renovation, and facilities improvement programs. Contribute to the development and maintenance of the campus facilities master plan and standard operating procedures. Evaluate current and future facility needs and provide recommendations and options to support strategic campus planning. Oversee fleet vehicle maintenance, transportation services, shipping and receiving, and event setup activities. Manage grounds and landscape operations, including irrigation, fertilization, pesticide applications, and seasonal snow removal. Oversee housekeeping contract requirements and ensure campus facilities and grounds are maintained to an aesthetically pleasing standard. Manage physical plant and construction projects from planning through completion, including developing specifications, estimating costs, preparing bid specifications, and coordinating contracted services. Oversee outside contractors and ensure projects are completed in accordance with specifications, applicable requirements, and established timelines. Coordinate with code officials regarding required permits and inspections. Collaborate with the Design and Space Planner, Information Technology, and Planning and Construction teams on campus projects and furniture, fixtures, and equipment (FF&E). Manage significant operational and capital expenses while ensuring responsible use of resources. Participate in the Prescott Chancellor’s Campus Leadership Team and provide facilities expertise to campus leadership. Respond to after-hours facilities issues as required in this on-call position. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Engineering or a related field . Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in physical plant maintenance, facilities, construction, or engineering. Three or more years of supervisory experience, or a combination of education and experience commensurate with the requirements of the position. Demonstrated knowledge of facilities management and/or auxiliary services principles and practices. Knowledge of construction rules, regulations, and compliance requirements. Knowledge of RFP and bidding processes, as well as contractual terms and conditions. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret construction drawings and specifications. Ability to interpret financial reports and legal documents. Demonstrated ability to negotiate contract terms. Strong supervisory and leadership skills. Ability to exercise independent judgment, make decisions, and resolve problems with limited supervision. Preferred Qualifications Experience leading facilities operations in a complex campus, institutional, higher education, or similarly diverse environment. Experience managing multiple facilities trades and service functions simultaneously. Experience overseeing large-scale construction, renovation, or capital improvement projects. Experience managing contractors, consultants, and competitive bidding processes. Experience with strategic facilities planning, preventative maintenance programs, and long-term capital planning. Strong communication, negotiation, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Work Environment This position is based on the Prescott campus and requires the ability to work across indoor and outdoor environments and respond to facilities needs as necessary. The position is on call at all hours of the day , with minimal travel required. The position description notes exposure to changing weather conditions, confined spaces, and hazardous materials. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311978. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Industry-Expert-Research-Scientist--Center-for-Aerospace-Resilient-Systems--CARS---Daytona-Beach-Campus_R311844-1": {
      "title": "Industry Expert Research Scientist, Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems (CARS), Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nVariable time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems (CARS) is seeking globally recognized aerospace systems industry technical leadership experts to help strengthen and grow the CARS research portfolio, with a near-term focus on aerospace cybersecurity, AI, Quantum computing, CNS ATM / C5ISR research in the civil and defense aerospace, and space systems domains. These research positions will lead the acquisition and support the execution of high-quality research, contributing to advancing knowledge in enhancing aviation and aerospace resilient systems. CARS is seeking self-motivated leaders who collaborate effectively across industry and government stakeholders, and engage with faculty, staff, and students to pursue innovative research projects and contribute to the overall mission of the Center. All projects are focused on student-engaged research to fund PhD, Master's, and undergraduate student research activities. The Center’s mission is to be a world leader in the research and innovation of safe, secure, and resilient aerospace system solutions that meet the needs of our global aerospace community. Strong research-focused candidates eager to proactively identify and address key aviation and aerospace systems resiliency challenges are encouraged to apply. This position is funded through the researcher's externally secured research activities, and is designed for individuals, including retirees from industry or major institutions, who continue to conduct research through ERAU/CARS and independently secure grant funding to support their work while serving as Principal Investigator. Individuals may also serve as personnel supported by grants led by other CARS investigators. Position Levels: Depending on preparation and experience, the position can be set at various levels, including Research Scientist and Senior Research Scientist. These positions provide diverse opportunities for individuals at different career stages to become part of a dynamic team and contribute to CARS research initiatives in aviation and aerospace resilient systems. Research Scientist Serves as an independent scientific researcher or a collaborator on a multi-scientist research initiative and may have lead responsibility for discrete components of a larger project under the general direction of a senior or principal investigator and is expected to capture and lead research proposals that can significantly aid in a research center’s ongoing projects. Requires a minimum of 20 years of relevant industry experience. While a Ph.D. (or equivalent terminal degree in a relevant discipline) is valuable, leadership and innovation in industry-government/industry technology development and research are most important. Candidates must have a demonstrated record of research engagement, including the influence, capture and/or execution of relevant new technology development or research projects. Senior Research Scientist An accomplished and experienced professional researcher who conducts significant original research or serves as a senior collaborator on a multi-scientist research initiative, typically leading substantive aspects of the overall project under the general guidance of a principal researcher. A Senior Research Scientist is expected to capture and lead large-dollar-value research proposals that can significantly aid in a research center’s ongoing projects and may serve as a co-investigator and / or principal investigator of externally funded research grants. Requires a minimum of 30 years of relevant industry experience. While a Ph.D. (or equivalent terminal degree in a relevant discipline) is valuable, leadership and innovation in government/industry technology development and research are most important. Candidates must have a demonstrated record of research engagement, including the influence, capture, and/or execution of relevant new technology development or research projects. A Senior Research Scientist is expected to capture and lead large-dollar-value research proposals (greater than $1M/yr) that can significantly aid in a research center’s ongoing projects and may serve as a co-investigator and / or principal investigator of externally funded research grants. About the Embry-Riddle Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems: ERAU's Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems (CARS) is the Embry-Riddle research center dedicated to advancing aviation and aerospace resilient systems, focusing on highly connected aerospace systems & operations including cybersecurity, AI, integrated systems, and rapid prototyping, supporting commercial and defense industries. CARS is committed to collaborating with industry and government partners, providing innovative solutions to pressing resilience challenges. The Center's work spans a broad spectrum of systems-related domains such as: aviation & aerospace cybersecurity including cutting-edge tools for enhancing cybersecurity in the operational technology (OT) domains, artificial intelligence / machine learning (AI / ML) and data science / data analytics, software engineering, , Communications / Navigation / Surveillance Air Traffic Management (CNS ATM) and Command / Control / Communications / Computing / Cyber / Surveillance / Reconnaissance (C5ISR) technologies and systems, human-machine interfaces, virtual and augmented reality training systems,  airspace/airport modeling & simulation, including  civil and defense airspace systems.  The Center also maintains a vast historical Air Traffic database (archived since 1999).  CARS has a support staff in place to assist with proposal development and project management. CARS is at the forefront of driving resilient systems innovation to foster a safe, secure, and resilient future of the aviation and aerospace ecosystem. About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Qualifications Applicants with the following expertise are encouraged to apply: Candidate must have or be able to acquire a US security clearance. Aviation and Aerospace Systems Expertise in any of the following areas: Aviation / Aerospace cybersecurity domain knowledge Comprehensive knowledge of aviation and aerospace systems, operations, principles, regulations, and best practices. Understanding of cybersecurity risk assessment, vulnerability management, systems resiliency evaluation, and testing within the aerospace domain. Application of AI/ML and Quantum computing. Leadership and Collaboration Skills Demonstrated ability to foster collaboration among industry, government, and academic leaders.  Ability to work with and mentor students in CARS research efforts. Proven track record of bringing diverse stakeholders together to achieve common goals. Research Proficiency: Demonstrated background in research and data analysis. Experience in designing and conducting aviation and aerospace systems research. Innovation and Thought Leadership: Ability to promote and support innovation in aviation systems through new technologies, strategies, and practices. Demonstrated thought leadership in aviation and aerospace systems. Ethical and Professional Standards: Commitment to integrity, ethical conduct, and adherence to professional standards in aerospace systems-related work. Communication and Networking: Excellent communication skills to effectively convey aerospace systems concepts, research findings, and ideas to diverse audiences. Strong networking skills for building working-together relationships. Regulatory / Compliance and Systems Standards Knowledge: Familiarity with aviation and aerospace systems standards at the global and regional levels. Interdisciplinary Collaboration: Ability to work across disciplines to address resilience challenges, incorporating insights from engineering, human factors, policy, and other relevant fields. Data Analysis and Decision-Making: Strong analytical skills for interpreting systems data and making data-driven decisions to enhance resilience measures. Continuous Improvement Mindset: Willingness to adapt and improve strategies based on emerging trends, technologies, and lessons learned. Adherence to Core Values: Commitment to upholding the core values of integrity, innovation, and collaboration in all endeavors. Global Perspective: Awareness of and adaptability to the global nature of the aviation and aerospace ecosystem, considering diverse regulatory environments and cultural factors. Candidates possessing a diverse range of these expertise areas will be well-prepared to effectively contribute to the realization of CARS's vision, mission, and objectives aimed at advancing aviation and aerospace systems resilience. Additionally, candidates must demonstrate proficiency in generating financially viable and pertinent research proposals, followed by effective project execution upon securing contracts. A forward-looking perspective on the aviation and aerospace systems industry, coupled with strong verbal and written communication skills, is imperative. The capacity to thrive in industry, government, and academic environments is mandatory. Supervision and project management, conducted in a collaborative yet results-driven manner, are pivotal for long-term success.  Successful candidates for this role are individuals with a proven history of autonomously initiating and executing research outside of established research centers. Application process/requirements To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311844 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Research Statement Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .  Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Temporary-Certified-Personal-Trainer_R311843": {
      "title": "Temporary Certified Personal Trainer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     The Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University Fitness Center is seeking qualified and experienced temporary personal trainers with current and nationally accredited (NCCA-approved) certifications to provide personal training services as a part of our on-staff fitness team. Details: This is a 6-month temporary position   About us     For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professiona l staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Qualifications Required: Valid nationally accredited (NCCA-approved) personal training certification (NASM, AFAA, ACE, ACSM, NCSF, NSCA, NETA, etc. CPR/ AED/ First Aid certification within 60 days of hire Ability to maintain a consistent work schedule  Ability to maintain a minimum of three active clients (when demand permits)  Reliable transportation Effective communication skills Preferred: A minimum of one year of personal training experience To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311843 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full CV   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .      Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote---United-States/Student-Recruitment-Counselor_R311981": {
      "title": "Student Recruitment Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity: The Student Recruitment Counselor (SRC) is a full-cycle recruiter working with prospective students to provide them with accurate information allowing them to make an informed decision. They may represent the university on occasion at educational fairs and tradeshows, as well as other post-secondary enrollment events. Working within the Student Recruitment Division, the Student Recruitment Counselor assists with the development of recruitment plans to meet targeted projections by implementing innovative as well as effective recruitment tactics and initiatives. The Student Recruitment Counselor is responsible for creating and maintaining relationships with prospective students through matriculation; assisting prospective students inquiring about various educational opportunities available through the Worldwide/Online Campus; manage projects as assigned; and assisting other departments such as admissions and advising as required. This position supports excellence in student services at every opportunity and seeks to continuously maintain a healthy relationship with university, military, and corporate affiliations. All SRC’s are required to utilize multiple resources and tools throughout their day to day activities for the purpose of effective recruitment.   Please note that due to staffing needs, this position is open to all candidates currently residing in, or planning to relocate to all states within the United States, with the exception of the following states:    California Washington Maine New York Oregon Colorado About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    The annual salary range for this role is up to $43,888 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.  Qualifications Must have a minimum of a high school diploma Must have a minimum of 1-3 years of excellence in Customer Service and/or 2 years of recruitment experience. 1-5 years of Financial Aid experience preferred.  Proven track record for consistently meeting deadlines with the ability to tactfully handle difficult situations and maintain composure under pressure, often under tight deadlines. Must be a dynamic, motivated, and enthusiastic individual with professional recruitment experience in higher education. Must have analytical skills, and technical expertise with Microsoft operating systems, Outlook/email, and Internet end-user applications including Salesforce. Must demonstrate exceptionally strong verbal and written communication skills. Must demonstrate a high standard of personal conduct, professionalism, and integrity and the ability to maintain confidentiality is vital. Must be able to provide excellent customer service to coworkers, staff, students, faculty, and customers. Must be able to work independently with minimal supervision and demonstrate a willingness to seek guidance and direction as necessary for the performance of duties. Must demonstrate excellent organizational skills with keen attention to detail to ensure a high degree of accuracy of all content. Must be able to recognize and deal with priorities, recognize and perform duties not directly assigned. Must be able to investigate, problem-solve and take corrective action. Moderate travel required. Required Schedule/Availability (all times are EST): We are currently searching for someone available for at 9:00 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. EST., but you also need to be available Monday through Friday: 8:00 a.m. – 8:00 p.m. EST as needed. Requirements to be able to drive a university vehicle: Must possess and maintain a valid, US driver’s license. In some instances, a valid Class C (CDL) license may be required. Must meet the University’s standards for approved drivers. Unacceptable driving records (as stated in the Use of Equipment and Vehicles Procedure 1.17) include the following (for three years from the date of each occurrence): Three (3) or more at-fault accidents and/or moving violations in the previous 36 months. Two (2) or more at-fault accidents or two (2) or more moving violations in the past year. Conviction for driving while impaired (DWI, DUI within the last five (5) years). Conviction for death by vehicle, hit and run, racing, careless and reckless driving, implied consent in the previous five (5) years. Serious violations result in immediate disqualification and revocation of driver privileges. The following are examples of serious violations:   Speeding over 15 mph of the posted limit, driving under the Influence of alcohol or drugs, leaving the scene of an accident, reckless or careless driving, Use of vehicle in (drug trafficking, reckless homicide, soliciting), unlawful use of weapons, driving under suspension or revocation, fleeing a police officer, vehicle theft, Improper or illegal lane change, following too close, and passing a stopped school bus while stop sign is engaged.   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311981 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Academic-Records-Specialist_R311388": {
      "title": "Academic Records Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace     As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning nearly 120 global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university.     For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery.     As we launch our next century, we remain committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible.   The Opportunity   The Office of the Registrar at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University offers a collaborative and student-focused environment that values innovation, operational excellence, and a commitment to student success. As part of this dynamic team, you will play a key role in supporting the academic mission of one of the world’s leading universities in aviation and aerospace education. This position provides an opportunity for a motivated professional to develop administrative expertise, strengthen student records management skills, and grow their career within a high-performing academic services environment. Team members are committed to delivering high-quality service to students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders while supporting one another in a fast-paced and mission-driven setting. Key Responsibilities Student Records & Processing Process student record actions including registration, record updates, academic adjustments, and credit assignments Maintain and update student records within the Student Information System Research archived records and recreate missing information to produce official transcripts Apply transcript notations, academic standing updates, and other academic record entries Process National Student Clearinghouse updates as required Transcript Services Review, process, and deliver electronic and paper transcript requests using Parchment system software Determine eligibility for transcript release in accordance with FERPA and university policy Maintain and track pending transcript requests and ensure timely follow-up Communicate ineligibility or account issues with students and campus partners Customer Service & Communication Provide daily support to students, advisors, and stakeholders via phone and email regarding transcripts and records Deliver professional, accurate, and timely responses to inquiries Interface with federal, state, and local agencies requesting student educational records Validate requests and ensure compliance with FERPA and institutional policies Coordinate subpoena requests and required documentation with appropriate university offices Administrative Support Provide administrative assistance to committees and departmental initiatives as needed Collaborate with campus partners to maintain accurate historical academic records Support continuous improvement of records processes and service delivery     Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!   Health Benefits:   Experience comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, along with wellness programs that include preventive care and fitness memberships. Our flexible spending and health savings accounts simplify managing healthcare costs. Join a workplace that prioritizes your health—because your journey to wellness should be rewarding! Buckle up for a healthier, happier you!   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.     Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes an annual 6% gift of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.         Compensation   The hourly rate for this position is up to $17.15 . The final offer will consider the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, along with applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.       Qualifications Education: Associate’s degree preferred Area of Concentration: Business Administration, Office Administration, Higher Education, or related field preferred Experience: 1–3 years of clerical or customer service experience required Experience in administrative support, records management, student services, or related office environment preferred Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities: Strong knowledge of State, Federal, and University policies, including FERPA compliance Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, Microsoft Teams, student information systems, and third-party software applications Strong organizational, analytical, research, and problem-solving skills Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced, detail-oriented environment Strong written and verbal communication and customer service skills Ability to contribute to a positive, collaborative, and team-oriented work environment Self-motivated with strong attention to detail and sound judgment in handling sensitive information Licenses, Certifications, and Security Clearances: None required Application process/requirements   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number   R31138 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/Communications-Operations-Supervisor_R311951-1": {
      "title": "Communications Operations Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     The Communications Operations Supervisor provides functional and operational supervision for the Campus Safety & Security Communications Center and Information Desk. This position is responsible for ensuring reliable communications operations, consistent service delivery, and adherence to established departmental standards, procedures, and applicable regulatory requirements. The position exercises supervisory authority over communications operations through the establishment and enforcement of operational standards, development and maintenance of procedures and documentation, coordination of training and onboarding, administration of communications systems, and provision of operational direction and performance guidance to staff. While the position does not routinely serve as a full-time shift supervisor, it provides shift coverage when operational needs require and maintains functional supervisory responsibility for communications operations through training oversight, procedural enforcement, systems administration, and performance guidance. The position works collaboratively with peer supervisors to promote seamless and consistent service delivery across functional areas. The Communications Operations Supervisor operates with a high degree of independence within the assigned functional scope and reports directly to the Associate Director of Campus Safety & Security. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Communications Operations & Systems Oversight Maintain operational readiness of the Communications Center, including CAD, radio, telephone, and related communications systems. Coordinate communications system administration, vendor interactions, issue tracking, and related documentation. Monitor and support operational continuity during system outages, incidents, and critical events. Maintain required operational logs, records, and compliance documentation. Identify operational issues and recommend improvements to communications systems, processes, and service delivery. Training, Procedures & Standards Develop, maintain, implement, and enforce communications procedures, workflows, protocols, and reference materials. Coordinate onboarding, training, and continuing education for Communications Center staff. Provide operational guidance and performance input related to communications standards and expectations. Monitor staff adherence to departmental policies, procedures, and applicable regulatory requirements. Identify training needs and coordinate appropriate development opportunities for communications personnel. Front Desk & Shared Service Operations Work regularly at the Information Desk alongside service operations staff. Provide professional, customer-focused support to students, faculty, staff, visitors, and other members of the campus community. Serve as an operational point of contact during assigned coverage. Provide Communications Center shift coverage when operational needs require. Assist with resolving operational issues and ensuring continuity of front desk and communications services. Operational Coordination & Campus Engagement Coordinate communications activities with peer supervisors to support consistent and unified departmental operations. Support campus events, emergency operations, and other departmental service initiatives. Participate in meetings, committees, training activities, and cross-functional coordination efforts. Collaborate with Campus Safety & Security leadership and campus partners to identify operational needs and implement effective solutions. Support continuous improvement initiatives that enhance communications operations, customer service, and campus safety.     About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.        Compensation     The hourly rate for this role is   up to $ 28.00. The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Required Education High school diploma or GED required. Demonstrated ability to read, write, and perform basic mathematical calculations. Working knowledge of basic grammar and composition. Required Experience Three to five years of related work experience, preferably in an administrative, communications, public safety, or operational environment. Prior administrative or supervisory experience, including scheduling responsibilities, preferred. Required Licenses, Certifications, and/or Security Clearances Valid Arizona Driver’s License required. Must meet the University’s standards for approved drivers. Must successfully complete a criminal background check and drug screening. No felony convictions. Driving Record Requirements Unacceptable driving records, as defined by the University’s Use of Equipment and Vehicles Procedure 1.17, include the following within three years from the date of each occurrence: More than three moving violations and/or accidents within a three-year period. More than two moving violations and/or accidents within any one-year period. A major conviction within the previous three years, including, but not limited to, driving while intoxicated, leaving the scene of an accident, reckless driving, and/or homicide or assault by motor vehicle. Required Within One Year of Becoming a Supervisor Must obtain the following certifications within one year of assuming supervisory responsibilities: Association of Public-Safety Communications Officials (APCO) Communications Center Manager certification. APCO Public Safety Telecommunicator Instructor certification. IS-300: Intermediate Incident Command System (ICS) for Expanding Incidents. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Exceptional verbal and written communication skills. Administrative and supervisory experience, including staff scheduling and coordination. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Demonstrated problem-solving and decision-making abilities. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and other standard office technologies, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams. Ability to adapt to changing operational needs and priorities. Demonstrated initiative and ability to work independently. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with staff, leadership, campus partners, and members of the campus community. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment when handling sensitive operational information.     To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311951. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Atsugi-Japan/Associate-Director--PACOM-Training---Advising_R311964": {
      "title": "Associate Director, PACOM Training & Advising",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       The Associate Director, PACOM Training & Advising offers an exciting opportunity to provide strategic leadership across Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University’s PACOM region while directly contributing to student success and staff development. This role is ideal for a collaborative leader who enjoys developing people, strengthening operations, and creating consistent, high-quality student support experiences across a geographically diverse region. The Associate Director will have the opportunity to shape and enhance training and onboarding programs, including innovative Canvas-based learning experiences, while coaching and mentoring staff to strengthen their advising and operational capabilities. The position will also play a key role in identifying opportunities for process improvement, using data and feedback to evaluate training effectiveness, and implementing solutions that improve team performance and operational efficiency. This role provides significant cross-functional exposure and the opportunity to build strong partnerships with advising, financial aid, academic departments, military education partners, and other University stakeholders. As a subject matter expert in academic policies, military tuition assistance, and regional advising practices, the Associate Director will help ensure PACOM operations remain aligned with University standards and evolving student needs. The Associate Director will also contribute to major regional initiatives, including PACOM graduation activities, compliance efforts, and campus operational improvements. This is an opportunity for a visible, student-centered leader to make a meaningful impact by empowering staff, strengthening collaboration, and advancing a culture of continuous improvement across the PACOM region. Key Responsibilities Lead training and professional development for PACOM staff, including onboarding, coaching, mentoring, and needs-based training programs. Develop and maintain training resources , including Canvas courses, presentations, and procedural documentation aligned with University policies and systems. Evaluate training effectiveness using performance data, staff feedback, and other metrics to identify opportunities for continuous improvement. Build strong stakeholder partnerships with advising, financial aid, academic departments, military education offices, and other internal and external partners. Serve as a subject matter expert on academic policies, procedures, Curriculum Standards, and Air Force and Army tuition assistance processes. Address complex inquiries and escalations , providing timely, solutions-focused guidance to staff and stakeholders. Improve regional operations by identifying process efficiencies, streamlining workflows, and strengthening coordination across PACOM campuses. Collaborate on major regional initiatives , including the planning and execution of the PACOM graduation ceremony. Support compliance and accreditation efforts , ensuring campus operations align with University policies, regulatory requirements, and applicable standards. Promote a student-centered culture through staff development, collaboration, mentorship, and continuous operational improvement About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.        Qualifications Required Education Bachelor’s degree in leadership , Education, Counseling, or a related field . Required Experience 3–5 years of relevant experience in higher education, student services, advising, training, operations, or a related field. Required Skills, Knowledge & Abilities Familiarity with Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University operations, policies, and procedures . Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated knowledge of information systems and the ability to learn and apply new technologies. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications , including Access, Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook/Email, and Internet-based tools. Ability to design, develop, and deliver effective training programs for diverse audiences. Strong communication and presentation skills, with the ability to explain complex information clearly. Ability to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to identify operational needs, recommend improvements, and implement solutions that enhance efficiency and effectiveness To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311964. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Camp-Pendleton-California/Site-Advisor_R311940": {
      "title": "Site Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity      Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University – Worldwide is hiring a Site Advisor at Camp Pendleton, CA . The Site Advisor acts as the sole point of contact for Embry-Riddle at this location and is responsible for the academic and operational tasks of the Worldwide site. Duties include academic advising, budget, compliance, facility oversight, and University support (including community relations). This position supports and promotes excellence in student services and community interaction at every opportunity. Participates as a team member and supports our team environment.   Please note: This position is in-person located at the ERAU Camp Pendleton, CA site.  This position is not remote or hybrid.      About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.       Compensation     The hourly range for this role is up to $21.10 + $9.14 location stipend . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.  Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required  At least three years of professional level experience, preferably working with students  Demonstrated work experience juggling multiple priorities in a professional manner    Required Skills, Knowledge, Abilities  Excellent customer service skills and ability to convey professionalism in all interactions. Analytical skills with an in-depth knowledge of information systems and technical expertise with Microsoft operating systems, Excel, PowerPoint, Word, and Outlook/email, and preferably SalesForce experience.  Ability to learn new things and keep up with the pace of changing technology. Ability to engage and connect with a diverse range of individuals in a friendly, approachable, and enthusiastic manner. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to investigate, problem solve and make informed decisions. Working knowledge of office procedures and equipment.   Job Responsibilities Include:   Advisement & Student Services  Provide personalized advising and support for all assigned students  Assist students with course registration and degree planning  Counsel students regarding available options for financial aid, scholarships, tuition assistance, Veterans Affairs benefits, etc.  Proactively contact students upon admission, during enrollment, and at other critical times during their academic career  Enter and maintain accurate student records on university platforms to include Campus Solutions, Imaging, and Salesforce    Administration & Site Management  Build and maintain relationships with local stakeholders to include the educational services office and productively interact with applicable Education Services Officer. Collaborate with Senior Leadership and the Scheduling Department to coordinate onsite course offerings and proactively work towards course enrollment. Identify, attend, and facilitate local events to establish community contacts, promote ERAU programs, and connect with prospective students Works with Senior Leadership to liaise with appropriate governmental authorities, industry and community leaders, and internal departments to ensure compliance with applicable laws and regulations Develop, monitor, and manage the site’s fiscal year budget effectively. Oversee inventory and safeguard university assets. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311940 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .     Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
