    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Network-Engineer_R311749": {
      "title": "Network Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking a Network Engineer to join the Information Technology team. Reporting to the Director of Network Engineering, this position is responsible for designing, implementing, administering, and supporting the University’s enterprise network and voice infrastructure. This role supports a hybrid environment, combining remote administrative responsibilities with on-campus work primarily based in Daytona Beach, Florida, assisting with network implementation, maintenance, and operational support across campus data centers and communication systems. The ideal candidate will have experience working in enterprise network environments using Cisco and/or Aruba technologies, with strong knowledge of routing, switching, wireless networking, firewalls, load balancing, and secure network architecture. Experience in hybrid or cloud-connected enterprise environments is highly desirable. Successful candidates are analytical, adaptable, and committed to continuous improvement. They communicate effectively, collaborate across technical teams, and provide high-quality customer service while supporting strategic IT initiatives. Preferred certifications include CCNP, Aruba Certified Switching Professional (ACSP), or equivalent advanced networking credentials. Embry-Riddle offers a collaborative work environment, professional development opportunities, a flexible summer schedule, and a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement plans, and generous education benefits. Key Responsibilities Network Operations & Support Monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve critical network performance and functionality issues Provide timely updates to management on outages and incidents Enforce operational policies and procedures to ensure high availability and reliability Respond to work orders and maintain accurate documentation in help desk systems Provide hands-on support for daily voice and data network operations Ensure IT equipment complies with industry standards and best practices Provide alternative solutions when necessary Network Design & Infrastructure Projects Participate in planning and implementation of infrastructure projects Design and develop network strategies and management practices Evaluate network changes and assess impact across campus systems Install, maintain, and support large-scale LAN/WAN and telecom services Coordinate low-voltage connectivity for campus construction projects Collaboration & Technical Consultation Collaborate with IT teams for troubleshooting, system configuration, and support Provide consulting, problem resolution, and needs analysis for stakeholders Support application and infrastructure integration efforts Planning & Governance Attend IT meetings, briefings, committees, and task forces Contribute to strategic and operational planning across IT departments Other Duties as Assigned Perform additional responsibilities in support of departmental and institutional needs. This is a hybrid position based in Daytona Beach that requires occasional on-campus work. Ideally, candidates should reside within approximately one hour of campus to accommodate in-office responsibilities as needed. About us    For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professiona l staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.     Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Qualifications Required Education Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 5+ years of experience in the design, operations, troubleshooting, and administration of enterprise Cisco or Aruba network environments (LAN, WAN, Wireless, Firewalls) Demonstrated proficiency in the configuration and management of Cisco or Aruba network infrastructure Strong working knowledge of network test and diagnostic equipment Expert-level understanding of Layer 2 technologies (e.g., Spanning Tree Protocol, 802.1Q, LACP) Expert-level knowledge of routing protocols (BGP, EIGRP, OSPF) Experience with network monitoring and telemetry tools (SNMP, NetFlow, sFlow, etc.) Extensive knowledge of Internet and IP-based services (DHCP, DNS, etc.) Experience supporting voice network systems and protocols (VoIP, RTP, SIP) Working knowledge of Avaya IP telephony administration Understanding of structured cabling standards, including copper and fiber optic environments Experience with cloud networking concepts and administration (Azure, AWS, GCP) Ability to plan, implement, and support technical initiatives in a complex enterprise or higher education environment Strong understanding of current IT networking and telecommunications trends and best practices Excellent customer service skills with a professional and solution-oriented approach Strong organizational and documentation skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with ability to work across technical and non-technical audiences Ability to maintain a professional demeanor in a collaborative environment Ability to document processes, procedures, and technical workflows accurately Commitment to IT core values, including accountability, continuous improvement, teamwork, and adaptability To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311749. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .      Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
