    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Data-Governance---Analytics-Manager_R310867": {
      "title": "Data Governance & Analytics Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle: A Global Leader in Aviation and Aerospace   With vibrant campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ—along with a Worldwide network spanning roughly 120 global locations—Embry-Riddle proudly stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. Now celebrating our 100th year, we continue to lead innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students worldwide. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space prepare the next generation of leaders shaping the future of flight and beyond.       The Opportunity   Position Summary: The Data Governance & Analytics Manager serves as a strategic partner within the Institutional Research office, guiding the stewardship, accuracy, and effective use of institutional data across the university. Reporting to the Executive Director of Institutional Research & Data Governance, the Manager plays a central role in developing and implementing data governance practices, facilitating collaboration among data stewards and campus partners, and ensuring that data is stored, documented, and accessed in ways that support compliance reporting and informed decision‑making. The Manager works closely with stakeholders to clarify dashboard requirements and designs user‑centered, accessible visualizations aligned with institutional priorities. As a connector between technical teams, subject matter experts, and executive decision‑makers, the Data Governance & Analytics Manager helps ensure that institutional data is trusted, consistent, and responsibly leveraged to advance the university’s strategic goals. Key Responsibilities & Oversight Data Management & Governance: Implement a framework that outlines the authority and decision-making processes for data-related activities, and the appropriate management of institutional data. Engage governance teams by aligning subject matter experts, IT and IR specialists, data domain stewards, and other stakeholders in a matrix model. Ensure that the entire network has the resources and shared organizational structure to allow seamless building upon the work of others within the model. Facilitate communication and coordination among governance teams, subject matter experts, data stewards, IT, and other stakeholders. Develop and maintain a comprehensive catalog of dashboard-related data, including standards, definitions, lineage, and governance guidelines. Dashboard Strategy & Development: Define clear ownership by identifying primary stakeholders and data stewards responsible for maintaining visualizations. Develop and document a standardized process for requesting, prioritizing, and developing new visualizations to ensure alignment, avoid duplication, and promote consistency in data usage. Evaluate existing vendor-provided and internally developed dashboards to assess the effectiveness of current analytics tools and processes. Identify unmet needs, usability issues, and opportunities for consolidation, enhancement, or development to ensure analytics solutions remain relevant and actionable. Design and develop cross-functional and executive-level dashboards. Optimize Institutional Research Data & Content: Maintain and enhance the Institutional Research (IR) data portal, public website, and internal site, ensuring intuitive navigation and timely, accurate content. Ensure that IR dashboards are visually consistent, branded, user-friendly, and aligned with institutional priorities. Curate and maintain the IR data library, ensuring accessibility and version control of key institutional data assets.         Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!   Health Benefits:   Experience comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, along with wellness programs that include preventive care and fitness memberships. Our flexible spending and health savings accounts simplify managing healthcare costs. Join a workplace that prioritizes your health—because your journey to wellness should be rewarding! Buckle up for a healthier, happier you!   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.     Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes an annual 6% gift of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.       Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications:   Required: Master’s degree in Information Systems, Data Science, Higher Education, Public Policy, or a related discipline. 3–5 years of progressively responsible experience in data governance, data stewardship, institutional research, or data management within a complex organization. Demonstrated ability to interpret data within an organizational and functional context, ensuring accuracy, consistency, and appropriate use across stakeholders. Experience operationalizing data governance practices, including defining data standards, coordinating data stewards, documenting data definitions, and ensuring data quality. Proficiency with data visualization tools such as Tableau or Power BI, with a focus on user experience, clarity, accessibility, and data storytelling rather than complex technical development. Excellent communication, facilitation, and relationship‑building skills, with the ability to bridge technical and non‑technical audiences, and guide collaborative decision‑making around data. Familiarity with compliance‑related reporting requirements in higher education (e.g., IPEDS, accreditation, state and federal reporting) and the data structures that support them. Experience with content management systems and maintaining data‑focused websites or internal portals. Working knowledge of student information systems (PeopleSoft preferred) and related campus platforms (LMS, CRM, etc.), with the ability to understand how data flows across systems. Understanding of data warehousing concepts, ETL workflows, and data architecture sufficient to collaborate effectively with IT—without being a primary developer. Familiarity with data cataloging and governance platforms (e.g., Data Cookbook) and maintaining metadata that supports institutional consistency. Preferred: Experience coordinating cross‑functional teams in data-related initiatives without formal supervisory authority. Skill in translating business or academic questions into clear data requirements, documentation, and dashboard specifications. Demonstrated commitment to data accessibility, equitable representation in dashboards, and user-centered design principles.         Application process/requirements   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number   R310867 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Powidz-Poland/Campus-Director_R311546": {
      "title": "Campus Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace     As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning nearly 120 global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university.     For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery.     As we launch our next century, we remain committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible.   The Opportunity   The Campus Director (CD), Powidz, Poland is responsible for the overall leadership, administration, and operational management of a Worldwide Campus location. This includes oversight of academic advising and student success services, campus operations, budget and financial management, outreach and community engagement, and supervision of campus staff. The Campus Director serves as the primary on-site representative of the University, ensuring compliance with institutional policies, supporting student retention and enrollment goals, and maintaining strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders. This role requires close collaboration with Worldwide Campus Operations and Enrollment Development leadership to ensure effective delivery of programs and services and successful progression of students from enrollment through graduation. Key Responsibilities Student Advising & Success Provide comprehensive academic advising, including program selection, degree mapping, and graduation planning Monitor student progress and proactively support retention and at-risk student populations Process academic requests including waivers, program changes, transfers, and graduation applications Maintain regular communication with students through email, phone, and in-person meetings Ensure enforcement of university policies and maintain accurate student records and confidentiality Coordinate student support services including financial aid, VA, admissions, bookstore, and tutoring resources Promote student engagement opportunities including scholarships, honor societies, alumni programs, and career services Administrative & Campus Operations Oversee maintenance of accurate campus and student data in institutional systems Ensure campus is audit-ready through proper financial and recordkeeping practices Monitor and support campus budget execution, travel, and purchasing reconciliation Ensure classroom and facility readiness for instruction, including technology systems Maintain compliance with operational policies and safeguard university assets Supervise staff (where applicable), including hiring, onboarding, performance management, and development Outreach & Community Relations Represent the University at education fairs, military briefings, and community engagement events Build and maintain relationships with local education and military partners Promote University programs and services to prospective students and stakeholders Support enrollment outreach initiatives and campus visibility within the region Training & Professional Development Participate in required training programs, meetings, and institutional development activities Engage in University-wide initiatives including town halls, workshops, and training sessions Provide feedback to improve operational tools, processes, and training effectiveness Additional Responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned in support of campus operations and student success Location: Powidz, Poland – This is a fully on-site, in-person position.     Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!   Health Benefits:   Experience comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, along with wellness programs that include preventive care and fitness memberships. Our flexible spending and health savings accounts simplify managing healthcare costs. Join a workplace that prioritizes your health—because your journey to wellness should be rewarding! Buckle up for a healthier, happier you!   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.     Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes an annual 6% gift of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period.   Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.       Compensation   The annual salary range for this role is   up to $50,400 including an $8,000 location stipend. The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications:   Bachelor’s degree required (field of study varies) Master’s degree preferred Experience Requirements 1–3 years of relevant professional experience required Experience in higher education administration, student services, customer service, marketing, or related field preferred Supervisory or management experience strongly preferred Required Skills & Competencies Strong ability to work independently in a geographically dispersed environment Demonstrated leadership, supervision, and team development experience Excellent verbal and written communication skills Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving abilities Ability to maintain professionalism and composure under pressure Experience working effectively with students, staff, and external stakeholders Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, Access) and web-based systems Strong understanding of data management and reporting systems Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines consistently Additional Requirements Ability to travel to campus and partner sites as needed ( moderate travel required ) Must be able to work in alignment with campus operational hours and student service needs Strong commitment to student success, retention, and enrollment growth Ability to maintain confidentiality and comply with institutional policies and procedures Application process/requirements   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number   R311546 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .     Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Prescott-AZ/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Computer-Science---Cybersecurity--NTT---Prescott-Campus_R311238": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science & Cybersecurity (NTT), Prescott Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Computer, Electrical, and Software Engineering Department at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University in Prescott, AZ invites applications for a full-time non-tenure track faculty position as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Computer Science and Cybersecurity for the 2026-2027 Academic Year with review of applications expected to begin immediately. Interest and ability to teach introductory undergraduate computer science and cybersecurity courses and laboratories is essential, and experience with aviation/aerospace applications is highly desirable.  Quality teaching and laboratory instruction is the primary responsibility for this position.  Additional responsibilities of the position may include recruitment of students, advising and mentoring undergraduate students, course and program assessment and development, and university/community service.  Excellent interpersonal skills, written and oral communications skills, and a strong command of the English language are required. About the Department of Computer, Electrical, and Software Engineering The Computer, Electrical, and Software Engineering Department is a part of the College of Engineering. The College of Engineering also houses the Aerospace Engineering Department and Mechanical Engineering Department.  A Cyber Intelligence and Security degree program in the College of Business, Security and Intelligence includes an isolated cyber and computer forensics lab that offers collaborative project opportunities.  A Simulation Science, Games and Animation degree program in the College of Arts and Sciences includes a lab supporting VR/AR/XR development, motion and face capture, and welcomes collaboration.  There are many other opportunities for inter-departmental teaching and research.  Our fully accredited undergraduate engineering programs place students in aerospace companies and major university graduate schools across the nation.   Embry-Riddle: A Global Leader in Aviation and Aerospace With vibrant campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ—along with a Worldwide network spanning roughly 120 global locations—Embry-Riddle proudly stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. Now celebrating our 100th year, we continue to lead innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students worldwide. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space prepare the next generation of leaders shaping the future of flight and beyond. Click here to take a virtual tour of the Prescott Campus! Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!    Generous Time Off: Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: The successful candidate should have an earned doctorate in computer science with background in cybersecurity, or doctorate in cybersecurity with background in computer science, or a related field. A MS degree in computer science with extensive industry experience will be considered. Preferred areas of expertise for this position include Computer science, Computer security, Cybersecurity, AI/machine learning, Software QA/Testing, Software Quality Assurance/Testing, Human-Computer Interaction (HCI), Embedded systems. Significant industry, entrepreneurial and/or teaching experience would strengthen a candidate’s credentials, but recent graduates are also encouraged to apply. Priority consideration will be given to candidates who have prospective research contribution to the Center for Aerospace Resilience, one of the University’s established Centers of Excellence. Applicants must include three (3) references with contact information in the application. Letters of recommendation will be requested for shortlisted candidates.   Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311238 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Letter of application addressing all of required qualifications listed above Statements of (1) research; and (2) teaching philosophy and experience Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Assistant-Director-of-Residential-Education_R311666-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Residential Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity  Embry-Riddle is now hiring an Assistant Director of Residential Education in the Department of Housing and Residence Life at the Daytona Beach campus. The position requires the employee to reside on campus to ensure availability for 24/7 response to assistance requests while serving in the on call rotation. The staff member will be provided with a university owned apartment as part of this requirement. This role is designated as essential personnel for campus emergencies and crises, as determined by the Dean of Students. Responsibilities include the following: Staff Supervision and Development Supervise Residence Life Coordinators Facilitating weekly one on one meetings, bi-weekly staff meetings, and training Provide guidance and leadership to full-time staff on individual and team issues Provide corrective feedback and written accountability for staffing concerns and employment policy violations Manages the RLC on call schedule and communicates the schedule Residential Curriculum Implementation Responsible for the creation, implementation, development and assessment of educational priorities Serves as the primary author of all residential curriculum facilitation guides Design and create the outline for RA and resident student interactions Assigns activity and program responsibilities to appropriate team members Maintains high visibility in the residence halls by completing monthly area/facility tours Student Development and Training Development, coordination, and implementation of student staff training Developing learning outcomes and objectives for each training session Communicate training expectations and schedules to resident assistant staff Design and execute ongoing training opportunities throughout the academic year Assess individual training sessions Administrative Communicate and respond to parent/guardian concerns and questions Attend weekly and bi-weekly staff meetings Responsible for communicating on-going room changes to department staff as well as students involved in the residence halls Occasional night and weekend commitments as needed Crisis Response and Management Participate in the department on-call crisis response and management rotation Serve as Essential Personnel for any severe weather situations that will impact campus About us For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!   Generous Time Off: Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Personal Leave: Relax with 12 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.  Qualifications Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in student development, Higher Education, or related field Minimum of 3-5 years of related work experience in student support (housing or residence life) Experience designing and implementing training presentations and on-going development plans Preferred Qualifications: Experience with residential curriculum or community development models Experience with software for residential/community engagement Experience supervising professional and student staff To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site  and search for requisition number   R311666 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .  Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu  and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
